{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,7,1]],"date-time":"2026-07-01T04:59:10Z","timestamp":1782881950749,"version":"3.54.5"},"reference-count":18,"publisher":"American Geophysical Union (AGU)","issue":"7","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2010,4,14]],"date-time":"2010-04-14T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1271203200000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":13,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Geophysical Research Letters"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2010,4]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Tri\u2010axial accelerometer data from the Challenging Minisatellite Payload (CHAMP) satellite have revealed the thermospheric density and its variability in unprecedented detail. The data often contain regions of high density located in the cusp sector at high latitudes. In this paper we provide the first detailed explanation of a high latitude density enhancement observed by CHAMP, focusing on the August 24, 2005 interval. The Thermosphere Ionosphere Mesosphere Electrodynamics General Circulation Model (TIMEGCM) was driven by high\u2010fidelity high\u2010latitude inputs specified by the Assimilative Mapping of Ionospheric Electrodynamics (AMIE) algorithm, and reproduced the main features of the density enhancements. The TIMEGCM and AMIE provide a global framework for interpretation of the CHAMP densities. Our simulations reveal that the observed density enhancement in the dayside cusp region resulted from unexpectedly large amounts of energy entering the Ionosphere\u2010Thermosphere system at cusp latitudes during an interval of strong (+20 nT) B<jats:sub>Y<\/jats:sub>.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1029\/2009gl042143","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2010,4,13]],"date-time":"2010-04-13T20:01:01Z","timestamp":1271188861000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":79,"title":["Thermospheric density enhancements in the dayside cusp region during strong B<sub>Y<\/sub> conditions"],"prefix":"10.1029","volume":"37","author":[{"given":"G.","family":"Crowley","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"ASTRA  San Antonio Texas USA"},{"name":"Department of Physics and Astronomy UTSA  San Antonio Texas USA"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"D. J.","family":"Knipp","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"High Altitude Observatory, NCAR  Boulder Colorado USA"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"K. A.","family":"Drake","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"CIRES University of Colorado at Boulder  Boulder Colorado USA"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"J.","family":"Lei","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Aerospace Engineering Sciences Department University of Colorado at Boulder  Boulder Colorado USA"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"E.","family":"Sutton","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"AFRL  Hanscom Air Force Base Massachusetts USA"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"H.","family":"L\u00fchr","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Deutsches GeoForschungsZentrum  Potsdam Germany"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"13","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2010,4,14]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_6_2_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.2514\/2.3937"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_3_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/181GM20"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_4_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/JA094iA12p16925"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_5_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/95JA02584"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_6_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/2006JA012113"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_7_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/JA087iA08p06339"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_8_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/92JA00228"},{"ke